# File: tests/unit/test_changelog_structure.py
# Generated from: specs/223-reconcile-changelog-release-sections-after-parallel-delivery-and-guard-their-structure-with-a-test/requirements.md
Feature: CHANGELOG release sections are unique, ordered and non-empty

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Each released version appears once, newest first
    Given the checked-in CHANGELOG.md and VERSION
    When the release headings below "## [Unreleased]" are read
    Then every version appears exactly once in strictly descending semver order
    And the first release equals VERSION

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: No release section is empty
    Given the checked-in CHANGELOG.md
    When each release section is read
    Then every release section has at least one bullet

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Reconciliation keeps every entry
    Given the bullets of CHANGELOG.md at commit 353e275
    When they are compared with the reconciled CHANGELOG.md
    Then the sorted bullet lines are identical
    And each of the 30 reconciled issue references appears in exactly one bullet

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The structure checker rejects a broken changelog
    Given synthetic changelogs with a duplicate version, an ascending version pair, an empty release section, and a newest release that differs from VERSION
    When the structure checker reads each one
    Then it reports at least one problem for each
